  "geometryBasis": "The named castle multipolygon and two open interior courts fix the house and attached service ranges. The separately named Victorian Conservatory lies west of the main house and has its own mapped outline.",
  "sectionBasis": "The castellation, stepped wings, round turrets and sash-window groupings follow the verified 2023 photo and the Irish architectural inventory. The greenhouse photo establishes the central curved glazed cupola, white mullions and pavilions, and the county documents the slope above the Irish Sea.",
  "limitations": [
    "Standing country house and service ranges with the rose garden conservatory. The remote park outbuildings, garden planting, icehouse and interiors are outside the modeled footprint.",
    "Roof heights, proportions of minor rear openings and the exact grey render finish are approximate. The 13-bay frontage and slate roof concealed by battlements follow the national inventory and photographs.",
    "The conservatory uses its named footprint and the original photograph. Minor glazing divisions and the foundation bench are estimated."
